 ople on your block\, and leave the sidewalks cleaner than you found them. 
 We provide all the supplies: grabbers\, bags\, gloves\, and vests. Just we
 ar comfortable shoes and show up.\nWhat volunteers get:\n\nA free sandwich
 \, salad\, or drink and pastry from Another Cafe\, ready when the cleanup 
 ends\nA chance at free tickets to that evening’s 7:45 PM stand-up comedy
  show at Cheaper Than Therapy (533 Sutter St)\, a neighborhood comedy club
  around the corner from Union Square. Seats are limited each week and go t
 o volunteers who claim them at check-in.\n\nEveryone is welcome\, includin
 g first-timers\, families\, and drop-ins. Check in with a QR code when you
  arrive. (Comedy tickets are for volunteers 18+.)\nOrganized by neighborho
 od volunteers in partnership with Civic Joy Fund and SF Public Works.\n\nU
 pcoming Lower Nob Hill Weekly Cleanup w/ Free Lunch for Volunteers (SF) Ev
